# GitHub SSH Setup & Troubleshooting Guide

## 🔐 1. Generate SSH Key (if not already)

```bash
ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C "your_email@example.com"
```

Files created:

* `~/.ssh/id_ed25519` → **Private key (KEEP SECRET)**
* `~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub` → **Public key (SHARE THIS)**

---

## 📤 2. Add Key to GitHub

```bash
cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
```

* Copy the output
* Go to GitHub → Settings → SSH and GPG keys
* Click **New SSH key** → Paste key → Save

---

## 🔍 3. Check Current Remote URL

```bash
git remote -v
```

### If you see:

```bash
https://github.com/username/repo.git
```

❌ This uses username/password (token)

---

## 🔧 4. Switch to SSH

```bash
git remote set-url origin git@github.com:username/repo.git
```

---

## 🔐 5. Test SSH Connection

```bash
ssh -T git@github.com
```

Expected:

```
Hi username! You've successfully authenticated...
```

---

## 🚀 6. Push Code

```bash
git push -u origin main
```

✔ No password required

---

# 🛠️ Troubleshooting

## ❌ Still asking for username/password

👉 Cause: Remote is still HTTPS
✔ Fix:

```bash
git remote set-url origin git@github.com:username/repo.git
```

---

## ❌ Permission denied (publickey)

👉 Cause: SSH key not loaded
✔ Fix:

```bash
eval "$(ssh-agent -s)"
ssh-add ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
```

---

## ❌ SSH agent not running

✔ Fix:

```bash
eval "$(ssh-agent -s)"
```

---

## ❌ Wrong key being used

Check available keys:

```bash
ls ~/.ssh
```

---

## ❌ Bad permissions on key

✔ Fix:

```bash
chmod 600 ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
chmod 644 ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
```

---

## ❌ First-time connection warning

You may see:

```
The authenticity of host 'github.com' can't be established
```

✔ Type:

```
yes
```

---

# 🧠 Key Concepts

* SSH uses **keys instead of passwords**
* `.pub` file → goes to GitHub
* private key → stays on your machine
* SSH URL → `git@github.com:...`
* HTTPS URL → `https://github.com/...`

---

